0 @I6000000014329712734@ INDI
1 NAME Sigfrid Justina /Friestad/
2 GIVN Sigfrid Justina
2 SURN Friestad
2 _MARNM Svanes
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 PLAC Kintyre Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Kintyre
3 STAE ND
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1 APR 1917
2 ADDR
3 CITY Wildrose
3 STAE ND
1 DEAT
2 DATE 27 DEC 1995
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Baptised: July 1, 1917, Zoar Lutheran Church, Noonan, ND  [''U.S., Evangelical Lutheran Church of America, Records, 1875-1940'']
2 CONT
2 CONT Reinert Svanes came to Kintyre March 23, 1929 at the age of 18 from his native land in Egersund, Norway. His brother Carl and sister Hannah had come in 1923. Hannah had married Magnus Thompson so Reinert stayed with them and worke
2 CONC d for Magnus and John Beal for two years, herding and caring for 500 to 700 sheep, spending long hours on horseback nine months of the year. He also milked cows and delivered milk every evening to many homes in town. Those who wer
2 CONC e Swedes or Norwegians he spoke to in his native tongue, but gradually learned the American language. In the fall of 1929, Reinert hauled a load of hay to the road crew horses and mules for $1.00 a load. This is when Highway 34 wa
2 CONC s built. In 1930, when the Peavey Elevator was built, Reinert hauled gravel and did carpenter work. In the winter he unloaded coal from boxcars. Kintyre was a thriving town at this time. In the fall and winter there was always ent
2 CONC ertainment, shows, dances, etc. In June 1929, a big three ring circus was there for three days. On Sunday afternoons everyone gathered to watch the Kintyre baseball team play with neighboring towns. About 70 children attended the 
2 CONC Kintyre school. In 1931 Reinert took a farm job with Thorvald Friestad for two years where he learned farming in America. In 1933 he worked for Gus Kleppe and in the fall he worked for Ben Maland as a carpenter. He went back to No
2 CONC rway to spend Christmas with his family. He stayed until February of 1935. Then he joined his cousin Olaf and they farmed the Long Place together. They spent five years here as bachelor farmers. No crop in 1936 so Reinert took a j
2 CONC ob reconditioning the Kintyre Elevator, wages there being $3.50 per day. From this experience he built his own elevator in 1954. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the meantime, Sigfrid Friestad, daughter of Ole Friestad was in Minneapolis going to college and nurses training. Due to her mother's death, she came home and spent one year on the farm keeping house for her father and brothers
2 CONC . Reinert was still single and felt a nurse in the house would be an advantage, but Sigfrid had two more years of training to take so they weren't married until December 28,1940. They lived on the Vie farm for a year and then move
2 CONC d to the Ole Friestad farm for four years. Here Rolf, their oldest son was born in 1942. Another son, Glenn Ole was born, but died four years later. In 1945, they purchased the Bernard Swenson farm just north of Kintyre where they
2 CONC  have resided since. Their other children are Randi, Linda, Glenn, Wanda and Nancy. [''Kintyre, North Dakota 75th Anniversary, 1904-1979'', p.135, http://www.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~ndemmons/historykintyre.pdf]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1940 Krober, Logan Co., ND census: living w/ father and siblings.  Reinert Svanes lived nearby.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married December 28, 1940 to Reinert Svanes.
