1 NAME Einar Carleton /Oftedal/
2 GIVN Einar Carleton
2 _MARNM Oftedal
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 23 OCT 1918
2 ADDR
3 STAE MN
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 19 MAR 2007
2 ADDR
3 STAE MN
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Einar C. Oftedal, 88, Cottonwood, died Monday, March 19, 2007 at Avera Marshall Regional Medical Center, Marshall.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held Friday, March 23 at Christ Lutheran Church in Cottonwood with burial in the church cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Visitation will be held Thursday, March 22 from 4-7 p.m. at the church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Einar Carleton Oftedal was born Oct. 23, 1918 in Sandness Township, Yellow Medicine County to Ludwig and Sina (Holen) Oftedal. He was baptized Nov. 24, 1918 and confirmed June 11, 1933 at Silo Lutheran Church, which is now Christ 
2 CONC Lutheran Church in Cottonwood. Einar graduated from Cottonwood High School in 1937.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elsie Jappe on April 23, 1944. Together the couple farmed and lived on the family farm three miles north of Green Valley. The farm was dedicated as a Century Farm in 1994.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a lifelong member of Christ Lutheran Church and was a Garst Seed Corn dealer. He also was a member of the Minnesota Farm Bureau, and served on the Lyon County Farm Bureau Board; was a nine year participant in the Farmers Bu
2 CONC reau Idea Exchange; a member of the Corn Growers Association and the Minnesota Soy Bean Growers Association.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his two daughters, Janice Oftedal, Cottonwood and Diane (Dean) Milbrath, Lake Elmo; 11 nieces and nephews.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his wife Elsie in 2005 and a brother, George Oftedal.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Kulow Funeral Service, Redwood Valley Funeral Home, Redwood Falls) 
